SOAPBOX: This was another WQ6X QRP operation from WA6TQT's superstation in Anza.
SOAPBOX: The SFI being a lowly 106 made for challenging radiosport conditions.
SOAPBOX: Having access to Stacked Yagi's on 40 - 10 meters and an 80-meter 4-square
SOAPBOX: vertical array made WQ6X's QRP signal sound like 200+ watts.
SOAPBOX: The biggest problem experienced universally was QSB everywhere requiring
SOAPBOX: repeats. Unfortunately, many stations would give up after my 2nd repeat
SOAPBOX: request - what's the big hurry?
SOAPBOX: Wassup with RTTY operation EXACTLY on 14.100 QRM'ing the NCDXF beacon - that
SOAPBOX: is pretty LAME (and LiDDiSH) if you ask me. There is plenty of room on 20-meters
SOAPBOX: that we can give the 14.100 frequency plenty of room. I heard stations on 20
SOAPBOX: all the way up to 14.148.
SOAPBOX: There were many VK stations on Friday/Saturday, but none on Sunday.
SOAPBOX: There were no ZL stations heard this year - missing Zone 32. Eu was
SOAPBOX: also noticeably lacking on the West coast. JA participation also seemed
SOAPBOX: to be considerably less than last year.
SOAPBOX: This year's score was 1/2 of last year, largely due to near non-existent
SOAPBOX: 10-meters and 1/2 the contacts on 40-meters. At least I can say that
SOAPBOX: WQ6X made an appearance nonetheless.
SOAPBOX: Read all about it at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
